  "articleBody": "Deciding whether to tackle rug removal yourself or call in professional help can save you a lot of headache and potential damage. If you're dealing with a large rug, especially one that's heavily glued down, it's often a smart move to bring in the experts. Trying to detach a stubborn rug, particularly if it's broadloom or commercial-grade, can be a real workout and even dangerous if you're not using the right tools or techniques. Sharp tools are often involved, and heavy lifting is a given, so safety is a big consideration. Another key indicator is the condition of your subfloor. If you suspect there might be hidden problems like soft spots, water stains, or squeaks underneath, a professional can properly assess and address these issues before new flooring goes down. Leaving staples or adhesive behind is a common mistake that can affect your new flooring installation. HH Remodeling LLC has the experience to handle adhesive, tack-strip, and pad removal with care, ensuring your subfloor is protected and ready for whatever comes next. Don't hesitate to reach out if your rug removal project seems too big or complicated – we're here to help in the Denver area!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
